// =============================================================================
// 08: SLOW ROCK BALLAD JAM — 16-BAR CINEMATIC JOURNEY (Key of D / Bm — 64 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Epic 16-bar slow rock ballad backing track engineered specifically for soaring
// lead guitar solos (in the spirit of Pink Floyd, Gary Moore, Slash, and Eagles).
//
// 🎛️ LAYER ORDER: DRUMS -> BASS -> CHORDS -> SOMETHING ELSE (ARPEGGIO & ORGAN)
//
// 🎸 WHY THIS TRACK PERFECTLY MATCHES LEAD GUITAR:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. FREQUENCY SEPARATION (NO MUD):
//    All rhythm instruments (chords, bass, arpeggios) are low-pass filtered
//    below 1350 Hz. The entire 1.5 kHz – 6 kHz presence band is left 100% crystal
//    clear for your guitar's pickups, overdrive, string harmonics, and bends!
//
// 2. ZERO NERVOUS DRUMS (DEEP SUBSONIC ANCHOR):
//    No agitated double-kicks or rapid pounding! The kick drum is a deep, warm
//    heartbeat placed ONLY on beat 1 (LPF 200 Hz). The snare delivers a massive,
//    wet stadium hall crack on beats 2 & 4 with long tail decay.
//
// 3. 16-BAR NARRATIVE PROGRESSION (Bm to D Major):
//    Takes the listener on a breathtaking journey from dark minor melancholy
//    (Bars 1–8 in Bm) to glorious, soaring daylight (Bars 9–16 in D Major).
//
// 🎼 16-BAR HARMONIC ROADMAP:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • PART 1: B MINOR BALLAD (Bars 1–8: Weeping, Emotional, Reflective)
//   Bar 1 : [Bm]   -> Deep minor tonic anchor
//   Bar 2 : [A]    -> Melodic step down
//   Bar 3 : [G]    -> Emotional subdominant lift
//   Bar 4 : [Em]   -> Dark reflective warmth
//   Bar 5 : [Bm]   -> Minor home
//   Bar 6 : [A]    -> Step down
//   Bar 7 : [G]    -> Rising tension
//   Bar 8 : [F#7]  -> Dramatic harmonic minor dominant turnaround!
//
// • PART 2: D MAJOR ANTHEM (Bars 9–16: Triumphant, Soaring, Heroic)
//   Bar 9  : [D]   -> Radiant D Major opening! (Hit high major notes!)
//   Bar 10 : [A]   -> Strong dominant pillar
//   Bar 11 : [Bm]  -> Relative minor echo
//   Bar 12 : [G]   -> Stadium anthem lift
//   Bar 13 : [D]   -> Pure daylight
//   Bar 14 : [A]   -> Driving forward
//   Bar 15 : [Em]  -> Breath of emotion
//   Bar 16 : [A]   -> Turnaround preparing for next loop
//
// 🎸 MASTERCLASS SOLOING ROADMAP (EXACT FRETS & MOVES):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • Over Part 1 (Bm — Frets 7–10 / B Minor Pentatonic & Aeolian):
//    e |--------------------------7--10--|  (B, D)
//    B |--------------------7--10--------|  (F#, A)
//    G |----------------7--9-------------|  (D, E)
//    D |----------7--9-------------------|  (A, B)
//    A |----7--9-------------------------|  (E, F#)
//    E |--7--10--------------------------|  (B, D)
//
//   ★ Move 1: The Gilmour 15th-Fret Cry:
//     Fret 15 on B string (D note) bent up a whole step to E, held with wide vibrato.
//   ★ Move 2: The Weeping Gary Moore Release:
//     Release 15th-fret bend slowly down to D, slide down to fret 14 on G string (A note)
//     as the chord transitions to A!
//   ★ Move 3: The Bar 8 F#7 Leading-Tone Target:
//     On Bar 8 (F#7), target fret 11 on B string (A# note) for chilling harmonic tension!
//
// • Over Part 2 (D Major — Frets 10–15 / D Major Pentatonic & Sweet Box):
//    e |--------10--12--14--|  (D, E, F#)
//    B |--10-12-------------|  (A, B)
//    G |--11----------------|  (F# = Sweet major 3rd of D!)
//
//   ★ Move 4: The Daylight Lift:
//     Slide into fret 11 on G string (F#), strike fret 10 on B string (A), then bend
//     fret 12 on B string (B up to C#) over the A chord — pure melodic magic!
//   ★ Move 5: The Epic Climax:
//     Whole-step bend on fret 17 of high E string (A note bent up to B)!
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// ⚡ TRACK 1: "COMFORT & GLORY" (16-Bar Epic Slow Rock Ballad — 64 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// PERFORMANCE BUILD ORDER: DRUMS -> BASS -> CHORDS -> SOMETHING ELSE (ARPEGGIO & ORGAN)
//   Starts with DRUMS active laying down the deep, massive, non-nervous stadium groove.
//   Then bring in your layers one-by-one:
//   Line 104: Ballad Bass | Line 107: 16-Bar Chords | Line 110: Clean Arp | Line 113: Organ Swell

stack(
  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Gentle unhurried quarter-note hats (keeps time with zero clutter)
  s("hh*4").gain(sine.range(0.18, 0.32).slow(2)),

  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Massive stadium ballad snare on 2 & 4 with deep hall reverb
  s("~ sd ~ sd").room(0.85).decay(0.6).gain(0.68),

  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Grounding subsonic kick on beat 1 only (calm downbeat anchor, zero nervousness!)
  s("bd ~ ~ ~").lpf(200).gain(0.55),

  // 1. [DRUMS - ACTIVE] Ambient cymbal crash marking the 8-bar section changes
  s("cr ~ ~ ~").slow(8).gain(0.35),

  // 2. [BASS] Sustained Ballad Bassline (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[b1 ~ ~ ~] [a1 ~ ~ ~] [g1 ~ ~ ~] [e1 ~ ~ ~] [b1 ~ ~ ~] [a1 ~ ~ ~] [g1 ~ ~ ~] [fs1 ~ ~ ~] [d2 ~ ~ ~] [a1 ~ ~ ~] [b1 ~ ~ ~] [g1 ~ ~ ~] [d2 ~ ~ ~] [a1 ~ ~ ~] [e1 ~ ~ ~] [a1 ~ ~ ~]>").s("triangle").lpf(300).decay(1.4).gain(0.65),

  // 3. [CHORDS] Lush 16-Bar Slow Rock Ballad Chords (Bm to D Major Journey) (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[b2,d3,fs3] [a2,cs3,e3] [g2,b2,d3] [e2,g2,b2] [b2,d3,fs3] [a2,cs3,e3] [g2,b2,d3] [fs2,as2,cs3,e3] [d3,fs3,a3] [a2,cs3,e3] [b2,d3,fs3] [g2,b2,d3] [d3,fs3,a3] [a2,cs3,e3] [e2,g2,b2] [a2,cs3,e3]>").s("sawtooth").lpf(1050).room(0.85).decay(2.2).gain(0.38),

  // 4. [SOMETHING ELSE - ARPEGGIO] Delicate Clean Picking Arpeggio (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[b2 d3 fs3 b3] [a2 cs3 e3 a3] [g2 b2 d3 g3] [e2 g2 b2 e3] [b2 d3 fs3 b3] [a2 cs3 e3 a3] [g2 b2 d3 g3] [fs2 as2 cs3 fs3] [d3 fs3 a3 d4] [a2 cs3 e3 a3] [b2 d3 fs3 b3] [g2 b2 d3 g3] [d3 fs3 a3 d4] [a2 cs3 e3 a3] [e2 g2 b2 e3] [a2 cs3 e3 a3]>").s("triangle").lpf(1350).decay(0.5).room(0.7).gain(0.24),

  // 4. [SOMETHING ELSE - ORGAN] Warm Leslie Swell on Turnarounds (Press gcc here)
  // note("<~!7 [fs3,as3,cs4,e4] ~!7 [a3,cs4,e4,g4]>").s("sine").lpf(850).room(0.9).gain(0.28),
).cpm(64)


